  "question": {
    "text": "A diatomic gas $(\\gamma=1.4)$ does $100 \\mathrm{~J}$ of work in an isobaric expansion. The heat given to the gas is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$250 \\mathrm{~J}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$150 \\mathrm{~J}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$350 \\mathrm{~J}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$490 \\mathrm{~J}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "For Isobaric process\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{w}=\\mathrm{P} \\Delta \\mathrm{v}=\\mathrm{nR} \\Delta \\mathrm{T}=100 \\mathrm{~J} \\\\ & \\mathrm{Q}=\\Delta \\mathrm{u}+\\mathrm{w} \\\\ & \\Delta \\mathrm{Q}=\\frac{\\mathrm{F}}{2} \\mathrm{nR} \\Delta \\mathrm{T}+\\mathrm{nR} \\Delta \\mathrm{T} \\\\ & \\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{f}}{2}+1\\right) \\mathrm{nR} \\Delta \\mathrm{T} \\\\ & \\left(\\frac{5}{2}+1\\right) 100=350 \\mathrm{~J}\\end{aligned}$<br />SECTION - B"
  }
}